ory 4: Synchronization\n36: \n37: | # | Check | Severity |\n38: |---|-------|----------|\n39: | 4.1 | `set_flag`/`wait_flag` present between pipeline stages | Critical |\n40: | 4.2 | Correct events used (MTE2_V, V_MTE3, MTE3_MTE2) | High |\n41: | 4.3 | Buffer IDs match between set and wait | High |\n42: | 4.4 | No missing sync between copy and compute | Critical |\n43: \n44: ## Category 5: Verification\n45: \n46: | # | Check | Severity |\n47: |---|-------|----------|\n48: | 5.1 | Output verification present | High |\n49: | 5.2 | Reference computation is correct | High |\n50: | 5.3 | Tolerance is reasonable for dtype | Medium |\n51: | 5.4 | Multiple test shapes if applicable | Low |\n52: \n53: ## Category 6: Code quality\n54: \n55: | # | Check | Severity |\n56: |---|-------|----------|\n57: | 6.1 | Implementation matches design document | Medium |\n58: | 6.2 | No unnecessary hardcoded magic numbers | Medium |\n59: | 6.3 | Reasonable naming conventions | Low |\n60: | 6.4 | Launch function properly configured | Medium |\n61: \n62: ## Scoring\n63: \n64: | Score | Criteria |\n65: |-------|----------|\n66: | 9-10 | No critical/high issues; clean code |\n67: | 8-8.9 | No critical issues; minor high issues addressed |\n68: | 7-7.9 | No critical issues; some high issues remain |\n69: | < 7 | Critical issues present; must fix before acceptance |\n\n(End of file - total 69 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# pyasc Kernel Review Checklist\n\n## Category 1: Syntax compliance\n\n| # | Check | Severity |\n|---|-------|----------|\n| 1.1 | All code inside `@asc.jit` uses supported syntax only | Critical |\n| 1.2 | No `print`, `break`, `continue`, `lambda`, `yield` | Critical |\n| 1.3 | No `try/except`, `raise`, `with open` | Critical |\n| 1.4 | No `import`/`from...import` inside JIT | Critical |\n| 1.5 | No nested functions, `global`, `nonlocal` | Critical |\n| 1.6 | No class methods as kernels | Critical |\n| 1.7 | No `async def`/`async with` | Critical |\n| 1.8 | Variables initialized before conditional use | High |\n\n## Category 2: API correctness\n\n| # | Check | Severity |\n|---|-------|----------|\n| 2.1 | All APIs exist in documented pyasc surface | Critical |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-code-review/references/pyasc-review-checklist.md","text":"# pyasc Kernel Review Checklist\n\n## Category 1: Syntax compliance\n\n| # | Check | Severity |\n|---|-------|----------|\n| 1.1 | All code inside `@asc.jit` uses supported syntax only | Critical |\n| 1.2 | No `print`, `break`, `continue`, `lambda`, `yield` | Critical |\n| 1.3 | No `try/except`, `raise`, `with open` | Critical |\n| 1.4 | No `import`/`from...import` inside JIT | Critical |\n| 1.5 | No nested functions, `global`, `nonlocal` | Critical |\n| 1.6 | No class methods as kernels | Critical |\n| 1.7 | No `async def`/`async with` | Critical |\n| 1.8 | Variables initialized before conditional use | High |\n\n## Category 2: API correctness\n\n| # | Check | Severity |\n|---|-------|----------|\n| 2.1 | All APIs exist in documented pyasc surface | Critical |\n| 2.2 | API parameters match documented signatures | High |\n| 2.3 | Tensor positions correct (VECIN for input, VECOUT for output) | High |\n| 2.4 | Data copy direction correct (GM->UB or UB->GM) | High |\n| 2.5 | Element counts and offsets are correct | High |\n\n## Category 3: JIT decoration\n\n| # | Check | Severity |\n|---|-------|----------|\n| 3.1 | Kernel function has `@asc.jit` decorator | Critical |\n| 3.2 | Kernel function does not return a value | Critical |\n| 3.3 | Device helper functions return top-level only | High |\n| 3.4 | Compile options are valid if specified | Medium |\n\n## Category 4: Synchronization\n\n| # | Check | Severity |\n|---|-------|----------|\n| 4.1 | `set_flag`/`wait_flag` present between pipeline stages | Critical |\n| 4.2 | Correct events used (MTE2_V, V_MTE3, MTE3_MTE2) | High |\n| 4.3 | Buffer IDs