{"type":"text","timestamp":1788350782533,"sessionID":"ses_f9e00e30effeG1WmRf607aEAkT","part":{"id":"prt_06202f6bc001Tn1vxZITzyvXXW","messageID":"msg_06202b4cc001zSY2kZ8HhH2ijy","sessionID":"ses_f9e00e30effeG1WmRf607aEAkT","type":"text","text":"Now let me perform the systematic static review.\n\n## Static Review of `candidate.py`\n\n### Phase 1: Module shape contract check\n\n| Requirement | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `import torch` | OK (line 1) |\n| `import asc`, `import asc2` | OK (lines 3-4) |\n| `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform` | OK (line 6) |\n| `@asc2.jit` kernel | OK (line 12) |\n| Public callable `rms_norm` matching schema | OK (line 53-57): `rms_norm(x, gamma, epsilon=1e-6)` |\n| `ensure_npu_platform()` first in wrapper | OK (line 58) |\n| `torch.empty_like(x)` for output | OK (line 63) |\n| `kernel[cores](...)` launch | OK (line 70) |\n\n### Phase 2: Syntax compliance inside `@asc2.jit` (lines 12-50)\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| No `print`/`break`/`continue`/`lambda`/`try/except` | PASS |\n| No imports inside JIT | PASS |\n| No nested functions/`global` | PASS |\n| No Python `range()` over runtime values | PASS (uses `asc2.range`) |\n| No `math.*` calls | PASS |\n| No early `return` | PASS |\n| Variables defined before use | PASS |\n\n### Phase 3: asc2 API correctness\n\n| API | Usage | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `asc2.global_tensor` | `(ptr, [S*D])`, `(ptr, [D])` — 1-D rank-1 | PASS |\n| `asc2.copy_in` | `(gm, [off], [tile_d], real_shape=[n_d])` | PASS |\n| `asc2.copy_out` | `(tile, gm, [off], real_shape=[n_d])` | PASS |\n| `asc2.range` | Outer: `(block_idx(), S, block_num(), unroll_factor=2)` | PASS |\n| `asc2.range` | Inner: `(num_d_tiles)` | PASS |\n| `asc2.reduce_sum` | Scalar accumulator seeding and accumulation | PASS |\n| `asc2.full` | `[1, 64]` seed and `[tile_d]` broadcast | PASS |\n| `asc2.rsqrt` | Tile operation | PASS |\n| `.to(asc.float32)` / `.to(x_tile.dtype)` | Type promotion/demotion | PASS |\n| No `gm_barrier` kwarg | PASS |\n\n### Phase 4: Kernel parameter types\n\n| Parameter | Type | Required | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| x_ptr, gamma_ptr, out_ptr | `asc.GlobalAddress` | Yes | PASS |\n| S, D, num_d_tiles | `int` | runtime | PASS |\n| epsilon | `float` | scalar | PASS |\n| tile_d | `asc.ConstExpr[int]` | compile-time | PASS |\n\n### Phase 5: Scalar placement (tile has no `__rmul__`)\n\n- `xf * xf` — tile*tile PASS\n- `ss + reduce_sum(sq)` — scalar+scalar PASS\n- `ss_tile / D` — tile/scalar-right PASS\n- `... + epsilon` — tile+scalar-right PASS\n- `xf * gf * inv_rms_tile` — tile*tile*tile PASS\n\n### Phase 6: UB budget verification (TILE_D=2048, worst-case f16 path)\n\nPass 2 worst: 6 tiles visible (x_tile 4KB + g_tile 4KB + xf 8KB + gf 8KB + yf 8KB + inv_rms 8KB) = 40KB naive. With 1.6x factor = 64KB. With unroll_factor=2 doubled = ~128KB. 128KB << 253952B budget. **No UB overflow risk.**\n\n### Phase 7: All 20 case route verification\n\nAll 20 cases verified: D ranges 2-8192 (num_d_tiles 1-4), S ranges 231-1000003 (all > 72, so cores=72), dtypes f16/f32/bf16, epsilon 1e-12 to 1e-3. Tail handling via `real_shape=[n_d]` covers all non-aligned D values (14 cases). No case exposes an uncovered path.\n\n### Phase 8: Numerical stability\n\n| Risk | Cases | Mitigation | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| f16 x^2 overflow (65504^2=4.3e9) | 19 | Promote to f32 before squaring | PASS |\n| f32 sum overflow (8192 * 4.3e9 ~ 3.5e13) | 5,11,19 | f32 range 3.4e38 | PASS |\n| All-zero input | 17 | eps=1e-4, rsqrt(eps)=100, y=0*gam*100=0 | PASS |\n| Tiny epsilon (1e-12) | 9 | f32 precision handles 1e-12 | PASS |\n| Catastrophic cancellation | none | Sum-of-squares is all positive | PASS |\n\n### Phase 9: Anti-cheat\n\n- No torch math ops PASS\n- No `.to(dtype)` on device data (kernel handles casts) PASS\n- No `torch.nn.functional.rms_norm` PASS\n- Output is fresh contiguous tensor, not a view PASS\n\n### Overall assessment: **Score 9/10 — No critical or high issues. Clean pass.**\n\nRunning compile-only syntax check:\n\n","time":{"start":1788350756540,"end":1788350782530}}}
